Z||000000||rodmcneill||02-16-2001||12:07 AM||||Is the shifting effort a lot higher when going with a short shifter? I have seen some shifters so short that they almost disappear. Am I better going with a straight shaft or more of the "dog leg" as on the 84 shifter? Pro's and con's on both?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||02-16-2001||12:32 AM||||Rod, It's all about what you want, " Its yo thang do what ya wanna do" to quote a song.<P>Yes, it is a little more effort the shorter it is, thus the "Competition Short Shifter"<BR>for gear banging. For a nicer look a straight<BR>rod will do, but it also can be a bit shorter than stock for a better feel.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
